---
// 隐私政策页(S05 站务页)。事实源 = tmp/app-store-launch/privacy-policy.md v0.3
// (中文定稿稿),本页为英译 + 两处增补(官网邮件订阅 Buttondown / 服务器运行日志
// 原始 IP 披露——2026-11-27 拍板走披露不动日志)。中/繁版对称维护于同目录。
// 「玄机问道」「QiCompass」一律不出现(HITL:定稿须用户过目后方可视为 published)。
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const lang = "en" as const;
const path = "/en/privacy";
---

<Base
  {lang}
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What KnowFate collects, where it goes, how it is stored and deleted — and what we promise not to do. No ad tracking, no data sales, no profiling."
  path={path}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <ol class="crumbs">
      <li><a href="/en">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">Privacy</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="policy">
      <h1 class="h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="caption">Effective date: to be set at publication. Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@knowfate.app">hello@knowfate.app</a></p>

      <p>We build KnowFate on one principle: <strong>collect only what a feature needs to run, and tell you plainly where it goes.</strong> This policy covers what we collect, how it is used, where it is stored, how to delete it, and what we promise not to do.</p>

      <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
      <p>The app works fully without an account. Signing in (Sign in with Apple / Google) is optional and only restores your charts and purchases across devices. To cast and read a chart you provide:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Birth information</strong> — date, time, sex, and birthplace (city, or longitude/time zone).</li>
        <li><strong>Ask-window content</strong> — the question you type and the preceding conversation.</li>
        <li><strong>Compatibility labels</strong> — the name you type for a comparison person (e.g. “mom”, “partner”).</li>
        <li><strong>Chapter feedback</strong> — your “accurate / not accurate” tap on a chapter (submitted anonymously); to prevent duplicate and abusive submissions the server stores a keyed digest of the IP, never the raw IP.</li>
        <li><strong>Abuse prevention</strong> — free quotas and ask-trial counts are keyed the same way (IP digest only, raw IP never stored); count records are kept for 7 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Cache identifier</strong> — a content hash derived from the birth information (not the birth information itself).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you sign in, the server additionally stores your user ID and email (returned by Apple on first sign-in / by Google on each sign-in) for account and purchase attribution.</p>
      <p>Payments: in-app purchases are processed by Apple's App Store. We never see your card details — only the validation result of a purchase receipt.</p>

      <h2>2. How information is used, and where it goes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Chart calculation</strong> — birth information is sent to our server to compute the chart (pillars, elements, luck cycles — calendar math). The computation happens during the request; the casting process itself does not store your birth information (except cloud-synced archives for signed-in users, see “Cloud sync”). The resulting chart data does become the input to the reading (below).</li>
        <li><strong>AI reading generation</strong> — readings are generated by third-party AI services, currently <strong>Z.ai (Zhipu) and DeepSeek</strong>. What is sent to them: chart data (pillars, elements, Ten Gods, luck cycles), birth time, birthplace (city), sex, almanac and hour derivations; your compatibility labels when comparing charts; and your question text with prior conversation when asking. <strong>Birth time, birthplace and sex are personal data in themselves.</strong> Compatibility labels and questions are typed by you — please avoid writing anything you would not send to an AI service.</li>
        <li><strong>Daily-fortune artwork (when enabled by configuration)</strong> — produced by a third-party image service from day-pillar and Ten-God imagery passed through a fixed lookup; it never includes birth time, sex, or birthplace as entered.</li>
        <li><strong>Cache</strong> — readings are stored in a server cache keyed by their content hash so they re-open instantly. <strong>The cache has no expiry and is kept indefinitely</strong>; deletion is described in §4. The hash does not directly contain your birth information, but if the birthplace were known to be one of the cities in our database, exhaustive matching cannot be fully ruled out (a space on the order of hundreds of billions).</li>
        <li><strong>Cloud sync (signed-in users only)</strong> — chart archives are uploaded to our server so a new device can restore them; after signing out, new data is not uploaded.</li>
        <li><strong>Anonymous statistics</strong> — we use TelemetryDeck for anonymous usage statistics (event names and enum parameters, random session IDs). It never contains birth information, reading text, or questions, and does not track across apps.</li>
        <li><strong>Website mailing list</strong> — the launch-notification form on this website collects the email address you enter, used solely to send the one launch notice. It is handled by Buttondown, our newsletter provider; you can unsubscribe at any time, and unsubscribing removes the address from the list.</li>
        <li><strong>Server operation logs</strong> — the server keeps short-lived access logs that contain request time and the raw IP address, rotated automatically by size. They are used only for troubleshooting and abuse prevention and are not linked to your account.</li>
        <li><strong>On-device data</strong> — chart archives, reading history and ask-session records live on your device.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do <strong>not sell</strong> data to anyone.</li>
        <li>We do <strong>not run ad tracking</strong> and integrate no ad networks.</li>
        <li>We do <strong>not build user profiles</strong>; anonymous statistics are never linked to identity.</li>
        <li>We do <strong>not use</strong> your information for anything unrelated to the product's features.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Storage and deletion</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>On your device</strong> — chart archives, readings and ask-session records are stored locally. Clear them in the app under My → Reset charts (sign-in state, language and purchase records are kept — the in-app confirmation says exactly what); or <strong>uninstall the app, which deletes all of it</strong> (sign-in credentials live in the system keychain and may remain after uninstall).</li>
        <li><strong>Server cache and ask records</strong> — the backend keeps the reading cache (addressed by content hash) and the questions/answers of your ask sessions (questions addressed by a question hash tied to your account or device). <strong>Neither expires automatically; both are kept indefinitely.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Delete account</strong> (available since 2026-11-24) — signed-in users can delete their account themselves under My → Settings → Delete account. Deleted: the account and credentials, synced charts (including birth data), ask credits and records, <strong>text you personally entered</strong> (question texts, compatibility labels, free-text fields in the health/wealth chapters) and their cache entries, and quota counters. Kept: an anonymized transaction ledger — purchase transaction IDs, product and date (for refund checks and duplicate-charge prevention, with account and chart identifiers removed). Reading cache entries derived purely from a chart — which anyone could regenerate — are not deleted with the account. Purchased chapters and ask credits cannot be restored after deletion (the confirmation dialog says so).</li>
        <li><strong>Cloud-synced data (signed-in users)</strong> — uploaded chart archives are stored on the backend and cleared together with “Delete account” (above). To clear cloud charts while keeping your account, contact us (§8).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. About AI-generated content</h2>
      <p>Readings are generated by AI from deterministic chart results. They are reference material within the traditional fate-calculation framework — not medical, psychological, legal or investment advice. The relevant disclaimer is shown on every results page in the app.</p>

      <h2>6. Children</h2>
      <p>The app is rated 4+ and collects nothing targeted at children. Users of any age provide only the birth information listed above.</p>

      <h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes materially, we will announce it prominently in the app before it takes effect.</p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>Email: <a href="mailto:hello@knowfate.app">hello@knowfate.app</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .policy { max-width: 760px; padding-bottom: 72px; }
    .policy h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 40px 0 14px; }
    .policy ul { margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 1.2em; }
    .policy li { margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .policy li strong, .policy p strong { color: var(--ink); }
  </style>
</Base>
